**Read:** [Mineralogy — Dexter Perkins, open editions](../sources/Mineralogy-Perkins.lingua#r_3Y3EJ93EG4V7Q0TZBCRRXVNVKP), the entire book and exercises; [Petrology — Dexter Perkins, open textbook](../sources/Petrology-Perkins.lingua#r_6P7JBVJJ3P1BT6QKDGC7BN6VWV), the entire book; [Guide to Thin Section Microscopy — Raith, Raase, and Reinhardt](../sources/Guide-to-Thin-Section-Microscopy.lingua#r_2MH30T4MGW8YMVP9SA3Z7XCDSD), the entire guide; [Raman Spectroscopy for Mineral Identification — Bartholomew and Post](../sources/Raman-Mineral-Identification-Practical-Guide.lingua#r_3TQHZH1T2CDCQPTVVXSKJ5DCED), the entire guide; [Petrology — Timothy Grove, MIT 12.109](../sources/MIT-Petrology-12-109.lingua#r_6Q1GZJKSZXQBM4N19CTRYG64TG), the full public sequence; [Sedimentary Geology — John Southard, MIT 12.110](../sources/MIT-Sedimentary-Geology.lingua#r_7FWZZ66CT5G1FP2JPQMWRV1YHM), the complete notes; [Advanced Igneous Petrology — Timothy Grove, MIT 12.490](../sources/MIT-Advanced-Igneous-Petrology.lingua#r_3R0PJP97ZPE1RSGPPGY8WXXQZF), the full public graduate case/lab sequence.

Read all of Perkins's Mineralogy and Petrology using identified editions, including figures, exercises, and descriptive references. Read the entire Raith/Raase/Reinhardt microscopy guide in English or Portuguese and the whole Raman practical guide. Complete the public mineralogy/optical lab manual and Brock optical sequence, recording unavailable apparatus or substitutions explicitly.

Work MIT 12.109's full published notes/labs/assignments, Nelson's complete public petrology notes, and Southard's complete sedimentary-geology notes. The undergraduate preparation grows into MIT 12.490's graduate case/lab/readings sequence. Commercial or restricted readings are accessed separately through authorized means; an abstract does not stand in for a full primary argument.

Read the complete relevant BGS classification reports, diffraction manual, NIST microanalysis paper, Portuguese pseudosection article, and Lanari/Duesterhoeft review. Work named crystallographic pamphlets and the full model/tutorial papers used in the studies. Source breadth supports a sustained programme rather than an arbitrary reading-title collection.

**Work:** produce an integrated explanation connecting structure/composition, measured properties, methods, phase relations, textures, and geological history. Re-derive consequential calculations and revise early interpretations after later evidence. Distinguish what an idealized model demonstrates from what the specimen and complete primary studies establish.

These are content expectations for demanding completion, with ordinary links allowing a reader to start anywhere. No new software gate, personal assessment instance, or authoring ceremony is required. The following projects develop practical and research competence through sustained evidence-based work.

